<title>CANADA: Canada government cash balances rise in week.</title>
<headline>Canada government cash balances rise in week.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Canada's cash balances rose in the week that ended January 15, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>				     Wk to Jan 15 Chg on wk Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  26.95   -0.786    +0.793</p>
<p>Government cash balances	     7.62   +0.450    -1.152</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	463.13   +0.632    +6.267</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 133.10   -2.100   -25.600</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  33.43   +0.032    +2.128</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.  </p>
<p>   Chartered bank assets			 Nov	   Oct</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			 -13.40	-12.97</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar				672.34	658.20</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	     109.16	104.58</p>
<p>					   Nov 96     Oct 96     Nov 95</p>
<p>M1					  67.19	65.70	59.83</p>
<p>M2					 396.29     393.68     385.18</p>
<p>M3					 497.23     492.77     470.73</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
</text>
